      "writtenOn": "2022-07-13T15:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question. I had never looked into this before but I remember seeing docs with code blocks that you can copy but the shell prompt doesn\u0027t copy. Looking into it I found this [g3doc-markdown](go/g3doc-markdown#shell-code-blocks) doc but I couldn\u0027t find anything similar in the gitiles docs except for this section about [specifying bash in code blocks](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gitiles/+/HEAD/Documentation/markdown.md#scripting) but that doesn\u0027t appear to add the prompt.\n\nLooking through other examples it seems like sometimes lines begin with `(chroot) $` [[1]](https://crrev.com/bebee6c32dbc28804f0ebccf48b7fda5800e6c2a/docs/write_protection.md#enable-hardware-write-protection) [[2]](https://crrev.com/bebee6c32dbc28804f0ebccf48b7fda5800e6c2a/docs/fingerprint/fingerprint-debugging.md#software) [[3]](https://crrev.com/bebee6c32dbc28804f0ebccf48b7fda5800e6c2a/docs/fingerprint/fingerprint-firmware-testing-for-partners.md#build-the-autotest-codebase)), sometimes it is specified above the code block [[4]](https://crrev.com/bebee6c32dbc28804f0ebccf48b7fda5800e6c2a/docs/hammer.md#build-ec), and sometimes it is just in the text [[5]](https://crrev.com/bebee6c32dbc28804f0ebccf48b7fda5800e6c2a/docs/getting_started_quickly.md#building).\n\nMy preference is generally for the most explicit option `(chroot) $ ` because it\u0027s less likely to be misread but it does make copy/paste slightly more difficult. As long as we\u0027re keeping consistent with the one of the existing inconsistencies I think we\u0027re okay though. 😄",
      "parentUuid": "4aadd78a_c76acbaf",
